            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0411" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/319: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-02-15T12:00:00-04:00">February 15,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. Referring exchange of notes between Embassy and Chilean Foreign Office,
                    Embassy [<hi rendition="#italic">dated?</hi>] February 1, 1938,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d429-f1"/> pursuant to Department’s telegram No. 13, February 4, 4
                        p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d429-f2"/> regarding provisional duration of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> of January 6, 1938,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d429-f3"/> I have the honor to report that as Chilean Congress has
                    not ratified <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> the latter lapsed on
                    January 31, 1939. Foreign Office entirely agreeable that it be promptly signed
                    again, as of February 1, 1939, in accordance with concluding sentence of the
                    notes of February 1, 1938 cited above. Suggest instruction authorizing this at
                    early date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
